Vendored ION-DTN headers and compatibility shims
=================================================

The contributions build against every ION-DTN release from 4.0.0 (June
2020) to 4.2.0.  What differs between those releases, as far as the
contributions are concerned, is handled here.

bpP.h - ION's private Bundle Protocol header
--------------------------------------------

bpP.h is an internal header that ION does NOT install to its include
prefix, yet the CLA sources (mail, mqtt, mysql, quic, tcpv4) require it.
Verbatim copies are kept here so the contributions can be built against
an *installed* ION without needing an ION source checkout.

Provenance (NASA-JPL ION-DTN, bpv7/library/bpP.h, unmodified):

  bpP-4.0.1.h   tag IOS-4.0.1                  serves 4.0.0, 4.0.1
  bpP-4.0.2.h   tag IOS-4.0.2                  serves 4.0.2
  bpP-4.1.3s.h  tag ion-open-source-4.1.3s     serves 4.1.0 to 4.1.3s
  bpP-4.1.4.h   tag ion-open-source-4.1.4      serves 4.1.4
  bpP-4.2.0.h   tag ion-open-source-4.2.0      serves 4.2.0

bpP.h itself is a small switch that includes the copy matching the
installed ION, keyed on macros the installed headers are the first to
define: ION_IPC_ATOMIC_OPAQUE_DEFINED (ion.h, 4.2.0), FQN_MAX_LENGTH
(ion.h, 4.1.4), BP_VERSION (bp.h, 4.1.0) and BP_BIBE_REQUESTED (bp.h,
4.0.2).

The struct layouts these headers declare must match the installed
libbp/libici, or the daemons will misbehave at runtime.  Between 4.1.4
and 4.2.0, BpVdb's delDeltas[] changed from atomic_uint (4 bytes) to
ion_ipc_atomic_t (8 bytes) and VEndpoint gained appCookie, shifting
every field after them (e.g. BpVdb.plans, which tcpv4cla and quiccli
read); 4.1.4 grew BpVdb and VPlan, 4.1.0 grew BpVdb, and 4.0.2 shrank
ClProtocol, which the CLAs allocate.  Where one copy serves several
releases, those releases differ only in fields of Bundle, which the
contributions never allocate or read.  When adding support for a new
ION release, add its bpP.h as another copy and extend the switch rather
than editing an existing copy.

compat/ - headers ION forgot to install
---------------------------------------

ION before 4.1.3s does not install cbor.h and crc.h, though its own
bpP.h includes them and libici exports their functions.  compat/ holds
verbatim copies from ion-open-source-4.1.3s (identical to 4.1.3's; the
earlier releases' versions are subsets); configure adds compat/ to the
include path only when the ION prefix lacks cbor.h.

ioncompat.h - public API the older releases lack
------------------------------------------------

The few pieces of ION's public API that the contributions use and that
releases before 4.1.4 do not have, supplied as static inline functions
for those releases:

  getOwnFqnn(), putFqn()       node numbers before the IPN naming
                               transition (mysql, quic, tcpv4)
  cbor_encode_signed_int(),    CBOR major type 1 (bpsh)
  cbor_decode_signed_int()
  ion_network.h                parseNetworkEndpoint() and friends and
                               itcp_connect_dualstack(), getaddrinfo
                               based as ION's are (tcpv4)

Each piece is keyed on a macro the ION header that introduced it
defines (FQN_MAX_LENGTH, CborNegativeInteger), except ion_network.h,
whose presence configure tests in the ION prefix and reports through
ION_CONTRIB_HAVE_ION_NETWORK_H.  On 4.1.4 and later the header only
includes ION's own.
